<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 The regulations in 9 CFR part 92, &sect;&sect;92.430, 92.431, 92.522, and 92.523 (referred to below as the regulations),
set forth the conditions under which importers may qualify animals to enter the United States through the Harry S Truman
Animal Import Center (HSTAIC) in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Fleming Key, FL. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Because the demand for quarantine space at HSTAIC has traditionally exceeded the space available, the regulations
provide that a lottery will be held each year during the first 7 days of December, to determine the priority of applications
for the following calendar year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Information concerning the lottery and how to submit applications were provided in a notice published in the 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 on August 22, 1994 (59 FR 43091, Docket 94&hyph;081&hyph;1). This notice announces a time for the lottery, and a change
in the location. 
