<SUMMARY>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUMMARY:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 GIPSA announces the designation of Mississippi Department of Agriculture and Commerce to provide official inspection
and Class X and Class Y weighing services under the United States Grain Standards Act, as amended (Act). 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=4 -->
Note:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The Grain Inspection, Packers and Stockyards Administration (GIPSA) was established by the Secretary of Agriculture's
Memorandum 1010&hyph;1, which abolished the Federal Grain Inspection Service and the Packers and Stockyards Administration
and transferred the functions of those agencies to GIPSA. Secretary's Memorandum 1010&hyph;1 was issued pursuant
to Public Law 103&hyph;354, the Federal Crop Insurance Reform and Department of Agriculture Reorganization Act
of 1994.)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
