<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
Warner Kramer, AGED Secretariat, 1745 Jefferson Davis Highway, Crystal Square Four, Suite 500, Arlington, Virginia
22202.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FURTHER>
<SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
The mission of the Advisory Group is to provide advice to the Under Secretary of Defense for Acquisition and Technology,
to the Director Defense Research and Engineering (DDR&amp;E), and through the DDR&amp;E, to the Director Advanced
Research Projects Agency and the Military Departments in planning and managing an effective research and development
program in the field of electron devices.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Working Group B meeting will be limited to review of research and development programs which the military proposes
to initiate with industry universities or in their laboratories. The microelectronics area includes such programs
on semiconductor materials, integrated circuits, charge coupled devices and memories. The review will include
classified program details throughout.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
In accordance with Section 10(d) of Pub. L. No. 92&hyph;463, as amended, (5 U.S.C. App. II Section 10(d)(1988)), it
has been determined that this Advisory Group meeting concerns matters listed in 5 U.S.C. 552b(c)(1)(1988), and that
accordingly, this meeting will be closed to the public.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Dated: November 28, 1994.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<SIGNER>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=06 g=1 f=1 -->
