<!-- PJG ITAG l=04 g=1 f=1 -->
Alternate OSD Federal Register Liaison Officer, Department of Defense.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=66 g=1 f=1 -->
F051 AF JA A
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
System name: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Judge Advocate General's Professional Conduct Files.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
System location: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Office of the Ethics Administrator, Office of the Air Force Judge Advocate General, 1420 Air Force Pentagon, Washington,
DC 20330&hyph;1420; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Army-Air Force Exchange Service Headquarters, General Counsel, P.O. Box 660202, Dallas, TX 75266&hyph;0202; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Defense Commissary Agency Headquarters, General Counsel, Building P11200, Fort Lee, VA 23801; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Defense Logistics Agency, Judge Advocate, Alexandria, VA 22310&hyph;6130. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Judge Advocate's office at headquarters of major commands, field operating offices, and unified commands. Official
mailing addresses are published as an appendix to the Air Force's compilation of systems of records notices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Categories of individuals covered by the system: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Judge advocates (active duty, reserve, or guard), civilian attorneys employed by The Judge Advocate General's department
and civilian attorneys subject to the disciplinary authority of The Judge Advocate General who have been the subject
of a complaint related to their professional conduct.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Categories of records in the system: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Records include, but are not limited to complaints with substantiating documents; letters/transcriptions of complaints,
allegations and queries; letters of appointment; reports of reviews, inquiries, and investigations with supporting
attachments, exhibits and photographs; records of interviews; witness statements; recommendations; reports
of legal reviews of case files; reports of Advisory Committee reviews; congressional responses; memoranda; letters
and reports of findings and actions taken; letters to complainants and subjects of investigations; letters of rebuttal
from subjects; financial, personnel, administrative, adverse information, and technical reports.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Authority for maintenance of the system: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
10 U.S.C. 8037, Judge Advocate General, Deputy Judge Advocate General: Appointment and duties; RCM 109, Manual for
Courts- Martial 1984.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Purpose(s): 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
To assist The Judge Advocate General in the evaluation, management, administration and regulation of the delivery
of legal services by offices and personnel under his jurisdiction. To ensure the proper qualifications for the practice
of law are met and maintained by each attorney practicing under the direct or indirect supervision of The Judge Advocate
General. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
To ensure licensing agencies of the individual states (including the District of Columbia) and the various courts
that licensed Air Force attorneys are advised of adverse determinations documenting violations of the rules of professional
responsibility affecting an attorney's fitness to practice law, this in an effort to protect the Air Force and the
general public from substandard legal practitioners. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
To record the disposition of ethics complaints and to document ethics violations and corrective action taken.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Routine uses of records maintained in the system, including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
categories of users and the purpose of such uses: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In addition to those disclosures generally permitted under 5 U.S.C. 552a(b) of the Privacy Act, these records, or
information contained therein, may specifically be disclosed outside the DoD as a routine use pursuant to 5 U.S.C.
552a(b)(3) as follows:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
To federal and state agencies or bar associations charged with licensing and authorizing attorneys to practice law,
and to various courts authorizing attorneys to practice before said courts, in order to protect the public and ensure
the proper administration of justice.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
To current and potential governmental employers during authorized background checks to assist their efforts to
protect the public and ensure the proper administration of justice. The Air Force `Blanket Routine Uses' set forth
at the beginning of the Air Force's compilation of systems of records notices apply to this system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Policies and practices for storing, retrieving, accessing, retaining, and disposing of records in the system:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Storage:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Maintained in file folders, in computer, and on computer output products. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Retrievability: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Retrieved by name of individual.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Safeguards: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Records are accessed by person(s) responsible for servicing the record system in performance of their official duties
and by authorized personnel who are properly screened and cleared for need-to-know. Records are stored in locked
rooms and cabinets. Those in computer storage devices are protected by computer system software. Computers must
be accessed with a password.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Retention and disposal: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Retained in office files for three (3) years after year in which case is closed. Records are destroyed by tearing into
pieces, shredding, pulping, macerating or burning. Computer records are destroyed by erasing, deleting or overwriting.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
System manager(s) and address:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Office of The Judge Advocate General, Ethics Administrator, 1420 Air Force Pentagon, Washington, DC 20330&hyph;1420.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Notification procedure: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Individuals seeking to determine whether this system of records contains information on themselves should address
written inquiries to the Office of The Judge Advocate General, Ethics Administrator, 1420 Air Force Pentagon, Washington,
DC 20330&hyph;1420.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Record access procedures: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Individuals seeking access to records about themselves contained in this system should address written requests
to the Office of The Judge Advocate General, Ethics Administrator, 1420 Air Force Pentagon, Washington, DC 20330&hyph;1420.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Contesting record procedures: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Air Force rules for accessing records and for contesting contents and appealing initial agency determinations
are published in Air Force Instruction 37&hyph;132; 32 CFR part 806b; or may be obtained from the system manager.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Record source categories: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Information is received from individuals; federal, state and local authorities; other Air Force records; state
bar records; law enforcement records; educational records; complainants; inspectors; witnesses and subjects
of inquiries.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
Exemptions claimed for the system: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
None.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SIGNJOB>
