<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, Madrid, Spain; to acquire 100 percent of the voting shares of First State Bank, Wilmington, Delaware.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
B. Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (Zane R. Kelley, Vice President) 104 Marietta Street, N.W., Atlanta, Georgia 30303:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1. ISB Financial Corporation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, New Iberia, Louisiana; to become a bank holding company by acquiring 100 percent of the voting shares of Iberia Savings
Bank, New Iberia, Louisiana. Iberia Savings Bank is currently a mutual savings bank that will convert to a stock savings
bank prior to its acquisition by ISB Financial Corporation.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
C. Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (Randall C. Sumner, Vice President) 411 Locust Street, St. Louis, Missouri 63166:
