<SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=2 -->
SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
I. Background 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
The National Housing Act (12 U.S.C. 1701&hyph;1749aaa&hyph;5) (the Act) authorizes and governs the Department's
mortgage insurance program. Section 221 of the Act permits certain HUD-insured mortgagees to assign the original
credit instrument and the mortgage securing the credit instrument to the Secretary of HUD. Section 221(g)(4)(A)
sets forth the two requirements for mortgage assignment. The commitment to insure must have been entered into prior
to November 30, 1983. Secondly, the mortgage must not be ``in default at the expiration of twenty years from the date
the mortgage was endorsed for insurance.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Section 221(g)(4)(C), which was added by section 336 of the National Affordable Housing Act of 1990 (Pub. L. 101&hyph;625,
approved November 28, 1990), authorizes the Secretary to conduct a multifamily project mortgage auction in lieu
of accepting the mortgage assignments. Section 221(g)(4)(C)(ii)(IV) of the Act states that the Secretary ``[s]hall
accept the lowest interest rate bid for purchase that the Secretary deems acceptable.'' Section 221(g)(4)(C)(ii)(IV)
also mandates that ``[t]he 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Secretary shall cause the accepted bid to be published in the 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
On October 20, 1994, the Department conducted the fourth multifamily project mortgage auction. All 111 projects
mortgages in the auction were sold to one bidder. In accordance with section 221(g)(4)(C)(ii)(IV) of the Act, the
Department is publishing details concerning the accepted bid, as follows:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

