<ACTION>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
ACTION:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Notice of Intent to prepare an Environmental Impact Statement on a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
mining Plan of Operations for Newmont Gold Company in Eureka and Elko 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Counties, Nevada; and notice of scoping period and public meetings. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=59 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</ACTION>
<SUMMARY>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUMMARY:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Pursuant to section 102(2)(c) of the National Environmental Policy 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Act of 1969 and 43 CFR Part 3809, the Bureau of Land Management will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
directing the preparation of an EIS to be prepared by a third-party contractor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on the impacts of a proposed Plan of Operations for gold mining by Newmont 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Gold Company, in Eureka and Elko Counties, Nevada. The Bureau invites 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comments on the scope of the analysis.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</SUMMARY>
<DATE>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
DATES:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Scoping meetings will be held December 7, 1994, at the Bureau 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of Land Management, Elko District Office, 3900 E. Idaho, Elko Nevada, and on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
December 8, 1994, at the Holiday Inn, 1000 E. 6th St., Reno, Nevada, to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identify issues and concerns to be addressed in the EIS. Both meetings are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
scheduled from 7:00&hyph;9:00 pm. Representatives of Newmont Gold Company will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be available to answer questions about the Plan of Operations. Additional 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
scoping meetings may be held as appropriate. Written comments on the Plan of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Operations and the scope of the EIS will be accepted until January 3, 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A Draft Environmental Impact Statement (DEIS) is expected to be completed by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the summer of 1995, and made available for public review and comment. At that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
time a Notice of Availability of the DEIS will be published in the 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The comment period on the DEIS will be 60 days from the date the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Notice of Availability is published. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</DATE>
<FURTHER>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
FOR FURTHER INFORMATION CONTACT:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Scoping comments may be sent to: District 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Manager, Bureau of Land Management, P.O. Box 831, Elko, Nevada 89803. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ATTN: Bootstrap EIS Coordinator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For additional information, write to the above address or call Deb McFarlane 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at (702) 753&hyph;0200. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FURTHER>
<SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=2 -->
SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
 Newmont Gold Company of Carlin, Nevada, has 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submitted a Plan of Operations to re-open their Bootstrap open pit mine and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
initiate mining at the Tara open pit mine, located 1,500 feet south of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Bootstrap. The proposed mines and associated facilities are located in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
portions of Sections 2, 3, 10, 11, 14, and 15 of Township 36 North, Range 49 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
East, MDM; approximately 30 air miles northwest of Carlin, Nevada. Newmont 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
developed the Bootstrap open pit mine in 1974, and the heap leach facility in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1977. Operations were conducted through 1984. Newmont performed closure and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reclamation procedures on the leach facility during 1987 and 1988. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proposal is to re-open the Bootstrap pit and develop the new Tara pit, create 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
two new waste dumps, develop a new heap leach facility, and reroute and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upgrade the existing access and haulage roads. Following public notice and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comment, Newmont acquired a permit from the Army Corp of Engineers to divert 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Boulder Creek around the planned mining activities. Diversion construction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
has commenced on private land and is expected to be completed in early 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Previous surface disturbance was to 121 acres of public land and 153 acres of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
private land. Part of the proposed operation would be confined to previously 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
disturbed areas. Additional surface disturbance is anticipated on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approximately 802 acres of public land and 288 acres of private land. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The issues expected to be analyzed in the EIS include potential impacts to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cultural resources, wildlife, pit water quality, air quality, soils, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vegetation, hazardous materials, paleontology, and social and economic values. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Cumulative impacts will also be addressed. In addition, the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
resources will be analyzed: recreation and wilderness, geology, range 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
management, lands and realty, visual resources, and land use planning. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
analysis will be conducted by an interdisciplinary team. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A range of alternatives (including but not limited to alternative reclamation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measures and the no-action alternative) will be developed to address the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
issues. Mitigating measures will be considered to minimize environmental 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
impacts and to assure that the proposed action does not result in undue or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unnecessary degradation of public lands. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Federal, state and local agencies and other individuals or organizations who 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
may be interested in or affected by the Bureau's decision on the Plan of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Operations are invited to participate in the scoping process with respect to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this environmental impact analysis. These entities and individuals are also 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
invited to submit comments on the DEIS. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
It is important that those interested in the Plan of Operations participate in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the scoping and commenting process. Comments should be as specific as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
possible. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=15 g=1 f=1 -->
The tentative project schedule is as follows: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=15 g=1 f=1 -->
Begin Public Comment Period_December 1994 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Issuance of Draft Environmental Impact Statement_Summer of 1995 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
File Final Environmental Impact Statement_Winter of 1995/1996 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Record of Decision_Winter of 1995/1996 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Begin Construction of Operation_Spring of 1996 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Bureau of Land Management's scoping process for the EIS will include: (1) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Identification of issues to be addressed; (2) Identification of viable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
alternatives; (3) Notification of interested groups, individuals and agencies 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
so that additional information concerning these issues, or other additional 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
issues, can be obtained. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<SIGNER>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=06 g=1 f=1 -->
Rodney Harris, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SIGNER>
<SIGNJOB>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=04 g=1 f=1 -->
