<DOCTITLE>Vought Aircraft Company A/K/A LTV Aerospace &amp; Defense Company Dallas, TX; Notice of Revised Determination on
Reopening </DOCTITLE>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
On November 9, 1994, the Department, at the request of the company reopened its investigation for the workers and former
workers of the subject firm in Dallas, Texas. The initial investigation resulted in a negative determination on February
24, 1994 and was published in the Federal Register 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
on March 10, 1994 (59 FR 11326). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Findings on reopening show that a sufficient amount of aircraft subassembly work has been offloaded overseas and
imported back to the subject firm. Sales at the subject firm decreased in 1993 compared to 1992. Substantial worker
separations occurred at the subject firm in 1993 and 1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Further, several appropriate subdivisions (job families at Vought Aircraft, a/k/a LTV Aerospace &amp; Defense
Company in Dallas) have already been certified to TAA under petitions TA&hyph;W&hyph;30,166, TA&hyph;W&hyph;30&hyph;167,
TA&hyph;W&hyph;30,202, TA&hyph;W&hyph;30,249 and TA&hyph;W&hyph;29,856. These certifications will be terminated
and the workers will be covered under TA&hyph;W&hyph;29,206. Vought Aircraft workers certified under TA&hyph;W&hyph;28,470
are not affected by this notice. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Conclusion 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
After careful consideration of the new facts obtained on reopening, its is concluded that increased imports of articles
like or directly competitive with the aircraft subassemblies contributed importantly to the decline in sales or
production and to the total or partial separation of workers at the subject facility. In accordance with the provisions
of the Trade Act of 1974, I make the following revised determination:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
All workers and former workers of Vought Aircraft Company, Dallas, Texas, except workers certified under TA&hyph;W&hyph;28,470,
who became totally or partially separated from employment on or after October 6, 1992 are eligible to apply for adjustment
assistance under Section 223 of the Trade Act of 1974. The following certifications are terminated TA&hyph;W&hyph;30,166;
TA&hyph;W&hyph;30,167; TA&hyph;W&hyph;30,202; TA&hyph;W&hyph;30,249 and TA&hyph;W&hyph;29,856 effective
November 16, 1994. Certification TA&hyph;W&hyph;28,470 is not affected by this notice. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Signed in Washington, D.C., this 16th day of November 1994. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<SIGNER>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=06 g=1 f=1 -->
Victor J. Trunzo, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SIGNER>
