The National Science Board (NSB) is the policymaking body of the National Science Foundation (NSF). The Board consists
of 24 members appointed by the President, with the advice and consent of the Senate, for six-year terms, in addition
to the NSF Director 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ex officio
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
