<DOCTITLE>Draft NUREG: Issuance Availability</DOCTITLE>
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
On November 4, 1994 (59 FR 55299), the Nuclear Regulatory Commission published for public comment a draft report entitled
``Revised Analyses of Decommissioning for the Reference Boiling Water Reactor Power Station'' (NUREG/CR&hyph;6174).
The draft report, prepared for the NRC by Battelle Pacific Northwest Laboratories (PNL), presented the results of
a review and reevaluation of the 1980 boiling water reactor (BWR) decommissioning study which addressed technology,
safety and cost issues associated with decommissioning a large nuclear power plant.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A request has been made by the Nuclear Energy Institute (NEI), which is an organization responsible for establishing
unified nuclear industry policy on matters affecting the nuclear energy industry, to extend the comment period because
of the importance of the decommissioning funding criteria. The NRC has no objections to this request and has agreed
to extend the comment period from December 23, 1994 to January 20, 1995.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
As noted in the initial 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 notice (59 FR 55299), draft NUREG/CR&hyph;6174 should be viewed as a first step in developing a more parametric approach
to estimating decommissioning costs and comments on the usefulness of such an approach are requested.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Comments and suggestions on the draft NUREG/CR&hyph;6174 should be sent to the Rules Review and Directives Branch,
Division of Freedom of Information and Publications Services, Office of Administration, U.S. Nuclear Regulatory
Commission, Washington, DC 20555. Copies of the comments received may be examined at the NRC Public Document Room
at 2120 L Street, NW., (Lower Level), Washington, DC.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Copies of draft NUREG/CR&hyph;6174 may be purchased from the Government Printing Office, P.O. Box 37082, Washington,
DC 20013&hyph;7082, telephone (202) 512&hyph;2249 or (202) 512&hyph;2171. Copies are also available from the National
Technical Information Service, 5285 Port Royal Road, Springfield, Virginia 22161. A copy is also available for inspection
and/or copying for a fee in the NRC Public Document Room, 2120 L Street, NW. (Lower Level), Washington, DC.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Single copies of draft NUREG/CR&hyph;6174 may also be obtained by written request or telefax (301&hyph;504&hyph;2260)
from: Distribution Services, Printing and Mail Services Branch, Office of Administration, U.S.Nuclear Regulatory
Commission, Washington, DC 20555.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For further information contact George J. Mencinsky, Division of Regulatory Applications, Office of Nuclear Regulatory
Research, Mail Stop T&hyph;9 C24. U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission, Washington, DC 20555, telephone (301) 415&hyph;6206.
