<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Constitution 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article I_General
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This Association shall be known as ``The National Environmental Laboratory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Accreditation Conference'' (NELAC) and is sponsored by the United States Environmental 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Protection Agency (U.S. EPA) as a voluntary association of State and Federal Officials 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for the purpose of establishing standards to consolidate and make more uniform the laboratory accreditation process.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article II_Objectives 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The objectives of the National Environmental Laboratory Accreditation Conference are: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
A. Forum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
To provide a national forum for the discussion of all questions related to standards for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
environmental laboratory accreditation by officials of the Federal Government and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regulatory officials of the States, Commonwealths, Territories and Possessions of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
United States, their political subdivisions, and the District of Columbia. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
B. Mechanism 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
To provide a mechanism to establish policy and coordinate activities within the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Conference on matters of national and international significance pertaining to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
environmental laboratory accreditation standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
C. Consensus 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
To develop a consensus on uniform standards, laws, regulations and specifications for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
laboratory inspections, procedures, criteria, personnel qualification, testing, administrative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedures and enforcement. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
D. Uniformity 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
To encourage and promote uniformity of requirements and methods among jurisdictions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
E. Cooperation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
To foster cooperation among regulatory officers and between them and the manufacturing, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
industrial, business, academic, consumer, and other interests affected by their official 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
activities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article III_Membership 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Membership consists of two classes: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Active Membership
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Active membership is limited to officials actively engaged in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accreditation of environmental laboratories or environmental program officials who are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in the employ of the Government of the United States, the States, the Commonwealths, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Territories, or the Possessions of the United States, or the District of Columbia. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Contributors
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Contributors comprise representatives of laboratories, manufacturers, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
industry, business, consumers, academia, laboratory associations, industrial associations, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
laboratory accreditation associations, and other persons who are interested in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
objectives and activities of the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article IV_Officers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_Ex Officio Officers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Director
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The Director of the Environmental Protection Agency National Environmental Laboratory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Accreditation Program is the ex officio Director of the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Executive secretary. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Director of the Environmental Protection Agency National Environmental Laboratory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Accreditation Program designates a senior member of the Environmental Protection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Agency who is thoroughly conversant with laboratory accreditation to serve the National 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Conference as its Executive Secretary. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 2_Elective Officers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Elective officers of the Conference shall be: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=15 g=1 f=1 -->
Chair, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Chair-Elect, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Past-Chair, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Treasurer, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
6 members-at-large to serve on the NELAC Board of Directors. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The consecutive reelection of a Chair-Elect is prohibited; the Chair-Elect shall not serve 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on any committee other than the Board of Directors. Should the Chair-Elect for any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reason be unable or unwilling to be installed as Chair, his/her successor shall be elected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in the manner prescribed. In this event, the newly elected Chair-Elect shall be installed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as Chair. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Eligibility
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 1. Any Active Member in good standing shall be eligible to hold any office provided 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that the individual meets the other requirements set forth in the Constitution and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Bylaws. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. The Chair-Elect will be elected at the Annual Meeting one year prior to the term 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of service as Conference Chair. After serving one year as Chair-Elect, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
incumbent will succeed to the office of Conference Chair. Only a state official is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
eligible for election to Chair-Elect. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Nominations and elections.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 1. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Nominating committee.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Chair shall appoint a Nominating Committee consisting of the most recent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
active Past Chair as Committee Chair and six (6) active members, to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
geographically representative insofar as possible. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Nominations
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. a. The Nominating Committee shall submit one name for each elective office 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and present its recommendation as a slate to the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00146 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
b. Additional nominations for officers may be made from the floor at the Annual Meeting provided that prior consent
of the nominee has been obtained in writing and presented to the presiding officer at the time of the nomination. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
3. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Elections.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Officers shall be elected during a designated session of the Annual Meeting by a formal recorded vote of the members
in attendance and eligible to vote on Conference motions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
4. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Terms of office.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 a. The Chair, Chair-Elect, and Past Chair, shall serve for a term of one year or until their successors are respectively
qualified and elected or appointed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
b. The Treasurer will serve a term of three years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
c. The six Board of Directors members-at-large shall serve for 3-year terms; two elected each year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
d. All officers shall take office immediately following the close of the Annual Meeting at which they were elected.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
5. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Filling vacancies.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 In case of a vacancy in any of the elective offices, the Board of Directors shall fill the office by appointment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article V_Appointive Officials 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_Officials, Specific 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Conference Chair with the approval of the Board of Directors will appoint the following officials:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=15 g=1 f=1 -->
Parliamentarian 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Assistant Treasurer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Appointment.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The Conference Chair shall appoint other officials to conduct Conference activities. See Bylaws, Article V_Duties
of the Officers and Article VI_Committees. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Assumption of office.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All appointive officials shall take office immediately following appointment and will serve through the subsequent
Annual Meeting of the Conference unless otherwise specified by the Conference Chair, Constitution or Bylaws. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00147 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article VI_Meetings of the Conference 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
A. Annual Meeting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Annual Meeting of members shall be held each year. The agenda for this meeting shall include the election of officers,
reports from the various committees, task forces, study groups, and the Treasurer, other items pertinent to the Conference,
and presentation to the Membership of pending issues requiring action by vote. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Annual Meeting may include the presentation of technical papers, discussions, displays, or other events at the
discretion of the Board of Directors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
B. Interim Meeting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Interim Meeting of the Board of Directors and those Standing Committees designated by the Chair shall be held annually,
approximately six months prior to the Annual Meeting to develop the agenda and committee recommendations for presentation
to and action by the membership at the Annual Meeting. Draft resolutions and standards regarding environmental laboratory
accreditation which have been published in the 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and commented upon are discussed and modified as appropriate in the Interim Meeting. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
C. Special Meetings 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. The Conference Chair is authorized to order a meeting of the Board of Directors at any time deemed necessary by the
Chair to be in the best interest of the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. Other Committees of the Conference are authorized to hold meetings at times other than the Annual Meeting or Interim
Meeting provided that: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a. such meeting or meetings have been funded in the Conference budget approved by the Board of Directors, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
b. such meeting or meetings are approved by the Chair and funding is available within the approved budget or can be made
available. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
3. A quorum shall consist of a majority of the eligible voters. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
D. Rules of Order 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The rules contained in Robert's Rules of Order (Revised) shall govern the Conference in all cases to which they are
applicable, and in which they are not inconsistent with the Constitution or Bylaws or the special rules of the Conference.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00148 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article VII_Fees and Dues 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The annual Membership fees and the registration fees for the Annual Meeting are recommended by the Conference Management
and Funding Committee and shall be approved (and may be revised) by a majority vote of the Board of Directors at any official
meeting of that Committee. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article VIII_Amendments to the Constitution 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This Constitution may be amended, added to, or repealed at any Annual Meeting of the Membership under normal Conference
procedures. Proposed changes must be included in the agenda of the Board of Directors for the Interim Meeting, published
in the Recommendations of the Board of Directors in its Tentative Report, and discussed at the general session of the
Board of Directors at the Annual Meeting at which said changes will be voted upon. Amendments to the Constitution must
be approved by a minimum of a two-thirds vote in both the House of Representatives and the House of Delegates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article IX_Bylaws 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_Supplementation of Constitution 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This Constitution shall be supplemented by Bylaws which shall detail the methods of operation of the Conference.
Such Bylaws shall not be inconsistent with the provisions of the Constitution. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 2_Amendments and Repeals of the Bylaws 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Bylaws may be amended or repealed in the same manner as prescribed for the Constitution (See Article VIII). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 3_Renumbering 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Executive Secretary is authorized to renumber the Articles and Sections of the Constitution or Bylaws to accommodate
any changes made. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Bylaws 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article I_Application for Membership 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_Form of Application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Each application for membership or contributorship shall be submitted to the Executive Secretary. The application
shall be accompanied by the Membership or Contributor fee. The successful applicant's name will be added to the Conference
mailing list. Confirmation of Member or Contributor status will be mailed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article II_Fees, Membership Records 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_Fees 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The fees for annual Membership, Contributorship, as well as the registration fee for the Annual Meeting, are established
by the Conference Management and Funding Committee and are subject to approval and revision by the Board of Directors.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 2_Membership Year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00149 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Annual membership fees shall be payable by July 1 of each year and will cover the period July 1 to June 30 of the following
year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 3_Billing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Executive Secretary shall bill each Member and Contributor for yearly dues 2 months prior to the expiration of
the current membership year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 4_Evidence of Membership or Contributorship 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Membership certificates and cards of suitable design, bearing the insignia of the Conference shall be issued to the
Members. Contributor certificates of a noticeably differing design shall be issued to the Contributors. The Executive
Secretary shall advise the Treasurer of the count of new Members and Contributors and will forward the membership
monies for deposit in the Conference Account. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article III_Use of the Insignia 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The insignia of the Conference may be used or displayed only by members of the Conference unless expressly authorized
in writing by the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article IV_Board of Directors 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_Membership 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. The Board of Directors consists of the Director, Executive Secretary, Chair of the Conference, Chair-Elect, the
most recent still active Past Chair of the Conference, the Treasurer, and the six at-large members. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. The Nominating Committee in recommending candidates for the Board of Directors shall consider regional representation.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
C. The term of the Board of Directors runs from the adjournment of the Annual Meeting at which its members are elected
(or appointed) through the succeeding Annual Meeting of the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 2_Duties 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. The Board of Directors has leadership responsibility for the conference and is charged with guiding the Conference
in its primary mission of establishing standards for the accreditation of environmental laboratories. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. It generates the constitution and bylaws of the Conference, presents amendments, proposes changes in organizational
structure, and defines roles and responsibilities as appropriate, for approval of the membership. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
C. It establishes administrative procedures and policy on internal matters and serves as the policy and coordinating
body in matters of national and international significance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D. It holds accountable, reviews, and approves actions of all Committees. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
E. It utilizes the Standing Committees to resolve technical criteria issues regarding laboratory accreditation.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
F. It acts for the Conference in all routine or emergency situations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
G. It authorizes interim meetings of Conference Committees as necessary. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
H. It fills any vacancy in any elective office of the Conference caused by death, resignation or retirement from active
official service. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
I. It brings recommendations to the Conference for consideration and action as appropriate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00150 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article V_Duties of the Officers
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_Chair
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Conference Chair is the principal presiding officer at the meetings of the Conference and of the Board of Directors,
makes appointments to the several standing and administrative committees, and appoints other Conference officials
to serve during his or her term of office. All appointments will be made with the consent of the Board of Directors.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 2_Chair-Elect
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Chair-Elect will:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A. serve as acting Chair of the Conference and the Board of Directors in the event that the Chair is unable to carry out
the duties of that office;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. perform other duties assigned by the Conference Chair, including presiding over sessions of the meetings of the
Conference as assigned by the Conference Chair and assisting the Chair in the discharge of his or her duties; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
C. serve on the Board of Directors.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 3_Past Chair
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The most recent still-active Past Chair will serve on the Board of Directors and as Chair of the Nominating Committee
and perform such duties as may be assigned by the Board of Directors. The Conference Past Chair may preside over sessions
of the meetings of the Conference as assigned by the Conference Chair and assist the Chair in the discharge of his or
her duties.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 4_Executive Secretary
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Executive Secretary acts as the executive officer of the Conference, the secretary and executive officer of the
Board of Directors, and the non-voting secretary to each standing committee; keeps the records of the proceedings
of the meetings and manages the conference administration as prescribed in its administrative procedures.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 5_Treasurer
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Treasurer receives and accounts for all monies collected and pays all Conference bills certified by the Conference
Management and Funding Committee as correct. The Treasurer is an ex officio member of the Conference Management and
Funding Committee.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 6_Assistant Treasurer
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Assistant Treasurer shall assist the Treasurer in the discharge of his or her duties.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 7_Parliamentarian
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Parliamentarian shall assist in assuring meetings of the Conference are conducted according to Robert's Rules
of Order and any special rules adopted by the Conference.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article VI_Committees
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_General
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Each administrative committee will consist of five Active Members (except the Contributors Committee) appointed
by the Chair of the Conference to serve appropriate terms on a rotating basis or until a successor is appointed. All
committee members will be appointed the initial year for appropriate staggered terms to allow for subsequent appointment
to full terms.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Except for the Nominating Committee, whose chair will be the Conference Past-Chair, each committee annually selects
one of its members to serve as its chair, who may succeed himself or herself.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00151 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Each standing committee will consist of five members elected from the Active membership of the Conference to serve
5 years with one member being elected each year. All committee members shall be elected during a designated session
of the Annual Meeting by a formal recorded vote of the members in attendance and eligible to vote on Conference motions.
When necessary, an appointment will be made to any of the standing committees to fill a vacancy caused by death, resignation
or retirement from active service by a committee member. The appointment is for the unexpired portion of the member's
term. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 2_Administrative Committees
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Terms. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Conference Management and Funding Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The term of service will be three years; two members to be appointed each of two years and one the third year. 2. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Nominating Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The chair shall be the Conference Past Chair. Four members shall be appointed annually to serve one year. 3. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Membership Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The term of service will be two years. Two members will be appointed one year and three the alternate year. 4. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Auditing Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The term of service will be three years. Two members are to be appointed in each of two years and one in the third year.
5. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Liaison Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The term of service will be three years. Two members are to be appointed in each of two years and one in the third year.
6. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Contributors's Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee will consist of five contributors to serve two years. Three members will be appointed one year and two
in alternate years. B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Duties. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Conference Management and Funding Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee prepares the annual budget for approval by the Board of Directors, sets and collects annual membership
fees and conference registration fees, selects the place and dates of each Annual and Interim Meeting of the Council
and manages the logistic details of the Interim and Annual meeting, certifies to the Treasurer the correctness of
bills submitted to the Conference for payment, and publicizes the Annual and Interim Meetings. The Treasurer is an
ex-officio member of this committee. 2. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Nominating Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee presents a slate of nominees for all elective offices at the Annual Meeting. The names of these nominees
shall appear in the report of the Nominating Committee and be published in the Conference Announcement. 3. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Membership Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee initiates membership invitations and publicizes the Conference to prospective members. This committee
also provides coordination and participation of Contributors in all affairs of the Conference. 4. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fiscal Auditing Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee arranges for annual audits of the Conference books. This committee reviews audit reports to the Board
of Directors with recommendations as necessary to resolve discrepant audit findings or recommendations. 5. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Liaison Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee provides liaison with international organizations, federal agencies, other groups and organizations.
This committee provides and solicits information and develops a spirit of cooperation between NELAC and other organizations.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00152 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
6. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Contributor's Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee serves as the focal point for the Contributors. It solicits information from and provides feedback
to the Contributors and acts as liaison to the Board of Directors on Contributor matters. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 3_Standing Committees 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
General
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Standing Committee members serve for five years, one member being appointed annually. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Duties.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 1. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Program Structure Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee shall develop modifications to the scope, structure, and requirements to the tiers and fields of testing.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
The Accrediting Authority Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee provides the standards used by EPA to approve state authorities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
3. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality Systems Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee establishes and keeps current the key elements of QA/QC, including record keeping and staffing requirements.
The committee also defines uniform standards for each of the elements of QA/QC. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
4. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Performance Evaluation Testing Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee determines the requirements for the Performance Evaluation Program, generates the standards for
the Performance Evaluation samples, provides criteria for selection of the provider of the Performance Evaluation
samples and provides and updates the protocol for the use of the Performance Evaluation Program in the accreditation
of laboratories. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
5. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
On-Site Assessment Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee determines the training and experience requirements of the assessors, establishes the frequency
of inspection, generates the procedures for on-site visits and publishes these standards in a National Environmental
Laboratory Accreditation Manual. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
6. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Accreditation Process Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee generates and develops modifications for the accreditation process of environmental laboratories,
including the requirements for accreditation, procedures for suspension, revocation and denial of accreditation,
relative roles and responsibilities of laboratories and appeal processes. This committee considers matters concerning
reciprocity of accreditation and establishes the process for the approval of state/federal accrediting authorities.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
7. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Regulatory Committee. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This committee provides the Standing Committees with current information on federal regulations that impact laboratory
testing. This committee annually presents a report for conference action. Its scope embraces all matters regarding
the development and interpretation of uniform laws and regulations, the study and analysis of bills for legislative
enactment, and the establishment and maintenance of published guidelines and other effective means of encouraging
uniformity of interpretation and application of laboratory requirements. The Regulatory Committee shall also
provide uniform language to assist states in adopting the standards in state statutes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 4_Special Committees, Task Forces, and Study Groups 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Special committees, task forces, and study groups may be established by the Conference Chair as the need arises or
as requested by the Conference. Members will be appointed from the Active Members for as long as deemed appropriate.
Upon completion of its assigned task, such bodies shall be dissolved by the Chair of the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 5_Subcommittees 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Upon request of a committee, the Conference Chair may appoint a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subcommittee(s) to assist the committee in fulfilling its responsibilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00153 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
Article VII_Voting System
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All questions before a meeting of the Conference that are to be decided by a formal recorded vote of the Active Members
are voted upon in accordance with the following voting structures and procedures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 1_House of Representatives
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Official Designation.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 This body of officials shall be known as the ``House of Representatives.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Composition
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 1. Each State is authorized one official to serve as its representative at the annual meeting of National Environmental
Laboratory Accreditation Conference. The state representative shall be the Director of the State Environmental
Laboratory Accreditation Program or the highest level technically competent scientist knowledgeable about environmental
laboratory analysis and accreditation, or his/her designee. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. Each of seven EPA Assistant/Associate Administrators (OSWER, OAR, ORD, OW, OPPTS, OECA, and OROSLR) or his or her
designee may appoint two members, one from headquarters and one from an EPA region. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
3. Each other participating federal agency with responsibilities in the environmental laboratory field is authorized
to appoint one official to the House of Representatives. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
C. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Method of Designation.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Each representative is specified annually to the Board of Directors 120 days before the NELAC Annual Meeting. Accommodation
may be made for exceptions to this deadline. An alternate should be named prior to the Annual Meeting in case the designated
representative cannot attend.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 2_House of Delegates 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Designation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. All other State and Federal environmental officials (those not sitting in the House of Representatives) are grouped
as a body known as the ``House of Delegates''. The number of potential members is not limited. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00154 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirements.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 No other special requirements apply. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 3_Voting Rules 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Proxy votes. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Proxy votes are not permitted. Since issues and recommendations in the committees' interim reports are often modified
and amended at the Annual Meeting, the attendance of officials at the NELAC Annual Meeting and voting sessions is vital.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Method. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All voting is by show of hands, standing vote or machine (electronic). There shall be no voice voting. No abstentions
are permitted. NELAC Annual Meeting and voting sessions are mandatory. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
C. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Timing. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Voting by both Houses is simultaneous. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recording. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The voting system is designed to record the votes of the Representatives whether an electronic system, show of hands,
standing vote or other method capable of being tallied is used. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
E. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
These procedures (rules) apply only to the Annual Meetings of NELAC. However, only active members are permitted to
vote in committee or other meetings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 4_Committee Reports 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Alternatives that may be used in voting on the reports: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=15 g=1 f=1 -->
A. vote on the entire report; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. vote on grouped items or sections; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
C. vote on individual items, according to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=14 g=1 f=1 -->
1. committee discretion, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. on request by a voting delegate, with the support of 10 others. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 5_Floor Amendments 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Amendments. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Committee chairs are allowed to offer amendments on the day of voting to make editorial changes in their final reports.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Changes. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Substantive changes can be made at the request of House of Representatives or House of Delegates members and: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1. A majority of the voting delegates of each House must vote favorably before a proposed amendment can be accepted
for debate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. A two-thirds favorable vote of each House on the amendment is required for passage (the requirement for the minimum
number of votes in both Houses also applies). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 6_Seating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Arrangement. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The seating arrangement for voting sessions is shown in Figure 1. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Supervision.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The members of the Board of Directors will control placement and movement of delegates. The Executive Secretary will
count votes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 7_Voting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
At the conclusion of debate on a motion, there shall be a call for the vote by a show of hands, standing, electronic count,
or other tally method. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minimum Votes. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. House of Representatives. A minimum of one-half the participating agencies must cast their votes in favor of, or
in opposition to an issue for the vote to be considered official. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
2. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
House of Delegates. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A minimum number of votes, equivalent to one-half the number of participating agencies, must be cast in favor of, or
in opposition to an issue for the vote to be considered official. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
B. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motion accepted. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. If the minimum number of members of the House of Representatives votes Yea; and if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00155 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
2. A majority of the members of the House of Delegates votes Yea (the minimum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
number of Yea votes required). If the minimum number of votes required to pass 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or fail an issue is not cast in the House of Delegates, the issue will be determined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the vote of the House of Representatives. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
C. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motion rejected. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1. If the minimum number of members of the House of Representatives votes Nay. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
and if 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
2. A majority of the members of the House of Delegates votes Nay (the minimum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
number of Nay votes required). Should a tie vote occur, or if the minimum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
number of votes required to pass or fail an issue is not cast in the House of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Delegates, the issue will be determined by the vote of the House of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Representatives. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Split or tie vote. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
When the two Houses split on an issue or the minimum number of votes supporting or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
opposing an issue is not obtained in the House of Representatives, the issue is returned 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the standing committee for further consideration. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The committee may drop the issue or reconsider it for submission the following year. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
issue cannot be recalled for another vote at the same Annual Meeting. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 8_Procedures 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Conference officers and committees observe in all procedures the principles of due 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
process_the protection of the rights and interests of affected parties; specifically, they 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(a) give reasonable advance notice of contemplated committee studies, items to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered for committee action, and tentative or definite recommendations for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Conference action, for the information of all parties at interest, and (b) provide that all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
interested parties have an opportunity to be heard by committees and by the Conference. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Section 9_Changes in Organization and Procedure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Proposals for changes in organization or procedure of the Conference are not acted upon 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
until the Annual Meeting of the Conference following the Annual Meeting at which such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proposals are made. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

