<!-- PJG ITAG l=77 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
Signature
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Laboratory Management Representative
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Representative
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=77 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
Name
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Laboratory Management.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
4.2&blank;Period of Accreditation
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For a laboratory in good standing, the period for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accreditation within categories for methods or analytes will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be reevaluated yearly and will be considered to be ongoing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
once a laboratory has been accredited for that category, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
method, or analyte. The loss of accreditation for categories, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
methods or analytes will occur upon not fulfilling any of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions outlined below in the sections on maintaining 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accreditation and supervision, revocation and loss of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accreditation. Additionally, failure to pay the required fees 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as determined by the participating states within the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stipulated deadlines or by the stipulated dates will result in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
loss of accreditation. This information will be entered into 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the National Database. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
There is a separate process for accreditation for new 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
categories, methods and analytes (vide supra: Application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Process, 4.1.7). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Each year the National Environmental Laboratory Accreditation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Program will provide each laboratory with a current directory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with information on what categories, methods, and analytes for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which they are accredited. Additionally, new categories, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
methods, and analytes will appear on the actual certificate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that is reissued as these items are added and/or deleted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
during the year. All new categories will be included in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
updates to the database. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
4.3&blank;Maintaining Accreditation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Accreditation remains in affect until revoked by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accrediting authority, until discontinued by the accredited 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
laboratory, or until expiration of accreditation date. To 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintain accreditation, the accredited laboratory shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
complete or comply with elements 4.3.1 TO 4.3.7. Failure to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
complete or comply with these elements may be cause for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
downgrading or revoking accreditation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



