<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Method Blank:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A clean sample processed simultaneously with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and under the same conditions as samples containing an analyte 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of interest through all steps of the analytical procedures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Method Detection Limit (Analytical Detection Limit):
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minimum concentration of a substance (an analyte) that can be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measured and reported with 99% confidence that the analyte 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
concentration is greater than zero and is determined from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
analysis of a sample in a given matrix containing the analyte. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(40 CFR Part 136 Appendix B). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
National Database:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A database run by the Federal Government 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or its authorized agent that has public information readily 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
available to the states participating in the NELAP program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
It would include information regarding the current 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accreditation and accreditation process and status on a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
laboratory by laboratory basis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
NELAC:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 National Environmental Laboratory Accreditation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Conference. A voluntary organization of state and federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
environmental officials and interest groups purposed primarily 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to establish mutually acceptable standards for accrediting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
environmental laboratories. A subset of NELAP. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
NELAP:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The overall National Environmental Laboratory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Accreditation Program of which NELAC is a part. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
On-site:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The laboratory facility, whether fixed or mobile, in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the context of actually visiting the facility for evaluation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or review of its program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Reagent Blank (method reagent blank):
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A sample consisting of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reagent(s), without the target analyte or sample matrix, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
introduced into the analytical procedure at the appropriate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
point and carried through all subsequent steps to determine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the contribution of the reagents and of the involved 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
analytical steps. (Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
PBM:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 Performance Based Methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Participating Member:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A state or federal agency identified by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA as having met all the standards for an accrediting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authority to accredit environmental laboratories. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Performance Evaluation Program:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The aggregate of providing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rigorously controlled and standardized environmental samples 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to a laboratory for analysis, reporting of results, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
statistical evaluation of the results in comparison to peer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
laboratories and the collective demographics and results 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
summary of all participating laboratories. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Performance Evaluation Sample (PE):
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A sample, the composition 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of which is unknown to the analyst and is provided to test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whether the analyst/laboratory can produce analytical results 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
within specified performance limits. (Glossary of Quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Precision:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The degree to which a set of observations or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measurements of the same property, usually obtained under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
similar conditions, conform to themselves; a data quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
indicator. Precision is usually expressed as standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
deviation, variance or range, in either absolute or relative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
terms. (Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Preservation:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 Refrigeration and/or reagents added at the time 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of sample collection to maintain the chemical and/or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
biological integrity of the sample. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Pure Reagent Water: 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
Water in which an interferant is not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
observed at the MDL of the parameters of interest. (40 CFR 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Part 136) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality Assurance Plan:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A written description of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
laboratory's quality assurance activities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR941202-2-00213 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR941202-2-00098 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality Assurance:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 An integrated system of activities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
involving planning, quality control, quality assessment, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reporting and quality improvement to ensure that a product or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
service meets defined standards of quality with a stated level 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of confidence. (Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality Control:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The overall system of technical activities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whose purpose is to measure and control the quality of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
product or service so that it meets the needs of users. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality Control Sample:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 An uncontaminated sample matrix 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
spiked with known amounts of analytes from a source 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
independent from the calibration standards. It is generally 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used to establish intra-laboratory or analyst specific 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
precision and bias or to assess the performance of all or a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
portion of the measurement system. (Glossary of Quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality Control Validation Studies:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The formal study of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sampling and/or analytical method, conducted with replicate, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
representative matrix samples, following a specific study 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
protocol and utilizing a specific written method, by a minimum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of seven laboratories, for the purpose of estimating inter-laboratory precision, bias and analytical interferences.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Sample Container:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The specific requirements for sample 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
containers are to assure a representative samples and sample 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
integrity, e.g., septa vials, glass or plastic. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Sample Duplicate:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 Two samples taken from and representative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the same population and carried through all steps of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sampling and analytical procedures in an identical manner. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Duplicate samples are used to assess variance of the total 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
method including sampling and analysis. (Glossary of Quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs):
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A written document 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which details the method of an operation, analysis or action 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whose techniques and procedures are thoroughly prescribed and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which is accepted as the method for performing certain routine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or repetitive tasks. (Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Standing Committee:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A committee of NELAC involved with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
establishing the technical standards for accreditation of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
environmental laboratories. Currently, these are the Quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Systems, Performance Evaluation Testing, On-site Assessment, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Accreditation Process, Regulatory, Accrediting Authority, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Program Structure Committees. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Supervisor:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The individual designated as being responsible 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for a particular area or category of scientific analysis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
This responsibility includes direct day-to-day supervision of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
technical employees, supply and instrument adequacy and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upkeep, quality assurance/quality control duties and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ascertaining that technical employees have the required 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
balance of education, training and experience to perform the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
required analyses. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Surrogate:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A substance with properties that mimic the analyte 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of interest. It is unlikely to be found in environment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
samples and is added to them for quality control purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(Glossary of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Technical Employee:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 The designated individual who performs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the ``hands-on'' analytical methods and associated techniques 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and who is the one responsible for applying required Good 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Laboratory Practice notices and other pertinent Quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Controls to meet the required level of quality. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=3 -->
Trip Blank:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
 A clean sample of matrix that is carried to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sampling site and transported to the laboratory for analysis 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
without having been exposed to sampling procedures. (Glossary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of Quality Assurance Terms, QAMS, 8/31/92). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



