<!-- PJG STAG 4703 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(12) Provide support for at least 10 graduate students annually to assist with the provision of technical assistance
with an emphasis on recruiting students from traditionally underrepresented populations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
Selection Criteria for Evaluating Applications 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Under the Accessing School-to-Work and Postsecondary Environments_A Technical Assistance Effort competition,
the Secretary proposes to use the following selection criteria. These criteria were taken from 34 CFR 380.11 (a)&hyph;(e)
and 380.13 (f) and (g).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(a) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plan of Operation. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(10 points) The Secretary reviews each application to determine the quality of the plan of operation for the project,
including_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The extent to which the plan of management is effective and ensures proper and efficient administration of the
project; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) How the applicant will ensure that project participants who are otherwise eligible to participate are selected
without regard to race, color, national origin, gender, age, or handicapping condition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality of key personnel. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(15 points) (1) The Secretary reviews each application to determine the quality of key personnel the applicant plans
to use on the project, including_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The qualifications of the project director (if one is to be used); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The qualifications of each of the other key personnel to be used in the project; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The time that each person referred to in paragraph (b)(1) (i) and (ii) of this section will commit to the project;
and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) How the applicant, as part of its nondiscriminatory employment practices, will ensure that its personnel are
selected for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, gender, age, or handicapping condition.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) To determine personnel qualifications under paragraph (b)(1) (i) and (ii) of this section, the Secretary considers_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Experience and training in fields related to the objectives of the project; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any other qualifications that pertain to the quality of the project. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Budget and cost-effectiveness. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(5 points) The Secretary reviews each application to determine the extent to which_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The budget is adequate to support the project; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Costs are reasonable in relation to the objectives of the project. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Evaluation plan. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(10 points) The Secretary reviews each application to determine the quality of the evaluation plan for the project,
including the extent to which the applicant's methods of evaluation_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Are appropriate to the project; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) To the extent possible, are objective and produce data that are quantifiable. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Adequacy of resources. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(10 points) The Secretary reviews each application to determine the adequacy of the resources that the applicant
plans to devote to the project, including facilities, equipment, and supplies. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Evidence of need. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(10 points) (1) The Secretary reviews each application to assess whether the need for the proposed technical assistance
has been adequately justified. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The Secretary determines the extent to which the application_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Describes the technical assistance needs to be addressed by the project; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Describes how the applicant identified those needs; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Describes how those needs will be met by the project; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Describes the benefits to be gained by meeting those needs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(g) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Project design. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(40 points) (1) The Secretary reviews each application to evaluate the quality of the proposed technical assistance
project design. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The Secretary determines the extent to which_
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The technical assistance objectives are designed to meet the identified needs and are clearly defined, measurable,
and achievable; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



